-- title:
--   Every successful trace return is a transversal
-- statement:
--   Let $n,r\in\mathbb N$, let $o_1,o_2$ be Boolean query functions on subsets of $[n]$, and let $s$ be an annealing schedule. A paired state is a subset of $[n]\times\{0,1\}$; a restart cursor stores such a state, a tape position, and an attempt count. Fix any Boolean tape $t$, rational parameter $q$, rational defect multipliers $w$, and initial and final restart cursors $c,c'$. If the capped positive-time trace-return procedure succeeds with $c'$, then $$\operatorname{classify}(c'.\mathrm{state})=\mathrm{transversal}.$$ Here a transversal has exactly one labelled element from each pair $\{i\}\times\{0,1\}$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/meelgroup/counting-matroid/blob/dd16a4628fdb095c58fe0f3dfd8e353c6e97443c/CountingMatroid/Analysis/RestartPhaseTransversal.lean#L38-L119

